        "say": "Memory needs the user's consent first. Show the consent text and ask.",
        "data": {
          "project": "corthex",
          "consent": {
            "version": 1,
            "text": "CORTHEX memory, consent version 1.\n\n- When memory is on for a project, this device records your prompts and the agent's final answers in sessions that work in that project's folders, after removing secrets and the text you mark with <private>. Tool calls, tool results and files are not recorded.\n- To curate memory, the recorded turns, the project's current state and its item list are sent to Anthropic with the key in CORTHEX_MEMORY_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, to the model in the memory configuration, by default Claude Haiku 5.5.\n- To recall and to search, your prompts, search requests and memory items are sent to OpenAI with the key in CORTHEX_MEMORY_OPENAI_API_KEY, to make embeddings, by default with text-embedding-3-small.\n- The raw recordings, the search index and the logs never leave this device. Sync is off until you turn it on; then only the curated memory goes to a sync server that you run, through its HTTPS gateway.\n- Recordings are deleted after 100 days unless you set another period. You can leave folders or kinds of entries out, pin and forget items, turn memory off for a project, delete a project's memory or delete all memory.\n- Anthropic's and OpenAI's terms for their APIs govern what they do with the data they receive. The plugin sets no spending limit; its usage is in the memory status and in each provider's console."
          }
        },
        "confirm": "k3v9q2m7"
